provenance.prompt:
Use the referenced Echo Catwalk sprite art only for exact identity, uniform, color palette and scale; draw six new poses, not copied poses. Create a 1536×1024 transparent RGBA pixel-art sheet, strict three-column by two-row, row-major. Broad gutters, complete figures inside cells. No background, floor, court, hoop, text, props, ball, sphere or basketball.

Echo is the reference's compact adult human man: medium-brown skin, short spiky dark-teal curls, teal headband, close dark-teal beard, teal sleeveless jersey with deep-purple/black accents, teal shorts, black knee pads and teal-black shoes. Keep his male face, hair, beard, proportions and kit consistent, exactly two arms/hands/legs/shoes. Both hands empty; the game draws the separate ball.

Right-facing behind-the-back pass toward image-right. Six connected keyframes:
0 ready stance, empty hands near chest;
1 turns shoulder and gathers invisible ball at waist;
2 pivots away from target, ball-miming hand sweeps behind lower back;
3 RELEASE at simulation tick7: torso twisted, lead hand passes behind the hip and opens toward image-right, ball-hand empty;
4 arm follows through across the back and torso unwinds;
5 recover to balanced right-facing stance with hands down.

Make six distinct complete poses, no cropped limbs or hair. Focus on believable torso rotation and a readable low behind-back hand path. True transparent alpha-zero sheet and margins, no haze/checkerboard/matte. Crisp 1990s arcade pixel clusters. Return only the sheet.
